cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its verification data, please cite this release and the associated manuscript."
title: "Reproducibility package for Four-step projective recurrence in a dyadic Cauchy-MDS shear layer"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Episkoposian"
    given-names: "Sergo A."
  - family-names: "Grigoryan"
    given-names: "Svetlana A."
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-07-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/dyadic-cauchy-shear-screening"
keywords:
  - dyadic matrix
  - Cauchy-MDS matrix
  - diffusion layer
  - finite fields
  - projective recurrence
  - reproducible cryptography
abstract: >-
  Exact verification code and machine-readable certificates for a dyadic
  Cauchy-MDS shear layer. The package directly scans all 252 admissible
  parameters, verifies the representative Jordan and period data, checks an
  isolated AES linear reference under a coherent row-major serialization, and
  reproduces two independent MILP computations of the exact value 25 in the
  stated MDS-support relaxation.
